## Workflows
-I have made a change in the naming of workflows, the name is user defined and the type is the workflow type like calibration, simple_detect, etc.

- So as per my design, when the maintenance mode is enabled, the workflow type should be calibration and the name should be the name of the workflow under the field calibration_workflow in calibration workflow.
- to switch to maintenance mode, the user should click on the maintenance mode button and the workflow on cnode_handler should be set to calibration using the commands:
  - workflow.stop -> workflow.set calibration -> workflow.run
- when the user switches back to production mode, the workflow on cnode_handler should be set to the workflow type and name, by chosing from a popup showing list of workflows to choose from. Then later run the workflow using the commands:
  - workflow.stop -> workflow.set <workflow type> -> workflow.run
- when running commands, wait for 1 sec to ensure the command is executed.
- In the edit settings form , show the selection of inputs and outputs(Relays) as buttons like in I/O test page. but in a row.
- In the cameras Row, renmae the field Profile to Detection profile. Move the edit perspective button to the right of the detection profile dropdown.

